<title>RUSSIA: Russian Oct oil output down two percent yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Russian Oct oil output down two percent yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian crude oil output in October rose three percent on September but fell two percent on year-ago levels, State Statistics Committee figures showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The committee released the following data for energy production:</p>
<p>		     Jan-Oct 1996 output	 Oct 1996 output</p>
<p>		   in million    yr/yr	 percentage change on:</p>
<p>		     tonnes   percent change   Sept 1996  Oct 1995</p>
<p> Crude oil	  244	    -2		 +3	   -2</p>
<p> Refined oil	147	    -4		 +5	   -2</p>
<p> Gasoline	    22.3	  -5		 +2	   -6</p>
<p> Diesel		39.2	  -2		 +7	   +1</p>
<p>Heavy fuel oil</p>
<p>  (mazut)	    52.9	  -3		+11	   +4</p>
<p> Lubricants	   1.9	  -8		 -0.7	-18</p>
<p>Natural gas</p>
<p>(billion cubic</p>
<p>  metres)	   471	    +1		+19	   +3</p>
<p> Gas condensate     6.8	  -0.8	    +14	   -2</p>
<p>-- Peter Henderson, Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
